From: Peyton Howe <peyton@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: imx415: add the native size selection target

libcamera reads V4L2_SEL_TGT_NATIVE_SIZE to learn the size of the pixel array
and logs "Unable to get rectangle 3 on pad 0/0" and "The sensor kernel driver
needs to be fixed" every time a camera is opened without it (the property then
defaults to the active area).

The driver already reports its pixel array for the crop, crop default and crop
bounds targets. Report the same rectangle for the native size, which the
selection API defines as the sensor's pixel array with top and left at zero.

--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx415.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx415.c
@@ -1136,6 +1136,7 @@
 	case V4L2_SEL_TGT_CROP:
 	case V4L2_SEL_TGT_CROP_DEFAULT:
 	case V4L2_SEL_TGT_CROP_BOUNDS:
+	case V4L2_SEL_TGT_NATIVE_SIZE:
 		sel->r.top = IMX415_PIXEL_ARRAY_TOP;
 		sel->r.left = IMX415_PIXEL_ARRAY_LEFT;
 		sel->r.width = IMX415_PIXEL_ARRAY_WIDTH;
